Full Impact Analysis: What Changes When the Schema Changes
1. Files That MUST Change
| # | File | What Changes | Why |
|:--|:-----|:-------------|:----|
| 1 | **`drizzle/schema.ts`** | Add `reports`, `follows`, `hashtags`, `videoHashtags` tables. Add `searchVector` column to `videos` table. | This is the source of truth for the database structure. |
| 2 | **`drizzle/migrations/*.sql`** (auto-generated) | New SQL migration files created by running `drizzle-kit generate` | These contain the raw `CREATE TABLE` / `ALTER TABLE` SQL that modifies the actual database. |
| 3 | **`drizzle/migrations/meta/*.json`** (auto-generated) | Snapshot files updated by `drizzle-kit generate` | Drizzle tracks schema state via these snapshots. **Must be committed to Git** alongside the `.sql` files to avoid migration conflicts. |

